data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":727,"item_id":"msg_0b3fdeb5633d7879016b00f2fd374887d1a6a88d341dc269d8","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"actor\":\"lin\",\"decision\":\"develop\",\"ability\":null,\"reason\":\"No implemented interface converts stationary exertion into bodily warmth. Rest restores energy, and shelter reduces environmental cooling; neither is functionally equivalent. Lin currently has sufficient energy and satiety for a modest exertion operation, but its net effectiveness must be measured against actual cooling rather than promised. No equipment or material stock is required.\",\"specification\":\"Implement active-warming@1 through the current development handoff. Public interface active-warming: parameters {rounds: integer, minimum 1, maximum 6}, required [rounds], additionalProperties false; prerequisites: alive and personally mastered. Learning: 2 rounds for pacing and interpreting temperature feedback, separate from implementation and use. At each execution round require energy >=3, satiety >=20, and actual temperature below the existing physiological comfort threshold. Remain at the actual current coordinate; spend 3 energy, apply ordinary metabolism and environmental temperature processing exactly once, then add up to 0.35 temperature units, limited to the remaining gap below that comfort threshold. Do not lower a temperature already above that threshold or suppress environmental overheating. No recovery, healing, insulation, immunity or persistent heat reservoir. Maintain actor-bound operation state {remainingRounds,startPosition,consecutiveReliefRounds}; movement, incompatible action, unmet prerequisites or death cancels before further expenditure. Completed expenditures are not refunded; there is no material escrow. Resolve any pending round only once. Geometry remains the actor's existing shared collision footprint, without teleportation, new obstacles or room effects; environmental and shelter effects use actual location. Declare warming-started, warming-round-completed, warming-completed, warming-cancelled and warming-comfort-qualified events. Round events report energy spent, temperature before processing, environmental temperature change, exertion heat, final temperature and measured cold-discomfort difference from the same-round no-exertion counterfactual. Bind rendering and personal memory to these events. Depend on existing action scheduling, metabolism, temperature/comfort calculations, death cancellation and wellbeing source evaluation; do not approximate ambient cooling with a separate replacement model. Versioned migration initializes no active operations and preserves all existing state and source histories. Review/development advances no simulation time and grants no mastery.\",\"experienceReview\":\"Exercise has no automatic satisfaction award; effort can be tiring and may fail to offset cold. Actual sustained relief can nevertheless benefit the performer. After three consecutive completed warming rounds, emit warming-comfort-qualified only if each round measurably reduces actual cold discomfort relative to its no-exertion counterfactual, with no starvation or health loss and with satiety >=20. Subscribe the existing thermal-refuge source to this qualified event as an alternative route to the same functional source, not a new additive source: participant is the exercising actor; amount/cap 1, duration 6 rounds, shared 12-round cooldown, repeat amount 1, refresh without stacking. Preserve shared history across shelter and exercise routes. Requesting, studying, starting exercise or merely generating heat does not qualify. Physical wellbeing continues to derive independently from actual hunger, health, fatigue and temperature.\",\"visualReview\":\"Show a restrained stationary exercise animation only while execution is active, retaining the actor's real position and collision footprint. Display remaining rounds, actual energy expenditure and signed environmental/exertion/net temperature changes from warming-round-completed. Completion and cancellation stop the animation immediately, including on death. Do not depict fire, shelter, guaranteed warmth or recovery; show relief feedback only after the validated qualification event.\",\"learning\":2}]}","logprobs":[]}

